JustFit 2.6 builds on JustFit 2.3.1, originally derived from Splash 1.3.0.
Upstream: https://github.com/incoai/splash
Pinned upstream commit: 0d5a035ea26d1cc566e3c7ee4e08e5e06fa68cf7

This distribution contains modified runtime/frontend code and additional JustFit
workers, service integration and release tooling. See ORIGIN.json and CHANGELOG.md.
The upstream Apache-2.0 license, source/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and inline notices
are retained. Licenses of the Rust crates linked into the native binaries are in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.
Model weights are downloaded separately. Chip-specific ANE vision assets are downloaded separately on first use from a
pinned, hash-checked index, with their own provenance.

JustFit product identity: the modified engine is named justfit-engine; its GPU
libraries are justfit.metallib and justfit-verify16.metallib. The native public command
is justfit. Production broker/management infrastructure is deployed separately. These names do not imply upstream endorsement.
Published upstream model repository names and packed-weight format identifiers
are retained for compatibility. Modified source files carry JustFit notices.

PDFium runtime binaries use bblanchon/pdfium-binaries, PDFium 158.0.8125.0
(chromium/8125). Pinned provenance is in config/native-libraries.json.
Complete provider, PDFium and bundled third-party license texts are retained in
config/licenses/pdfium-158.0.8125.0.txt and runtime PDFIUM-LICENSES.txt.
PNG compression loads the macOS system zlib through dyld; it is not redistributed.
